\section{Systems Architecture}

The Cosmos-Harmony runtime is structured as a continuous, closed-loop
autonomous intelligence system composed of five tightly coupled operational
phases. Each phase transforms its inputs into mathematically verified outputs
that feed directly into the next stage, forming a planetary-scale feedback
cycle.

\subsection{Astrophysical Entropy Ingestion Layer}

At epoch $t$, the system ingests high-entropy cosmic telemetry:
\[
\eta_t = E(\text{PTA}_t, \text{CMB}_t, \text{GW}_t, \text{Solar}_t),
\]
where $\text{PTA}_t$ denotes pulsar timing array measurements, $\text{CMB}_t$
cosmic microwave background anisotropies, $\text{GW}_t$ gravitational-wave
background signals, and $\text{Solar}_t$ solar flux variance. This entropy
stream defines a neutral stochastic baseline used for randomization, scenario
sampling, and tie-breaking in global coordination.

\subsection{Post-Quantum Cryptographic Seeding Layer}

Each region $i$ possesses a private type vector $\theta_i$ encoding preferences,
capacities, and sovereignty constraints. These types are committed using
lattice-based cryptography:
\[
C_i = A\theta_i + r_i,
\]
where $A$ is a public matrix and $r_i$ is a random masking vector. Regions
generate zero-knowledge proofs $\pi_i$ certifying that proposed controls
$u_{i,t}$ satisfy Ex-Post Incentive Compatibility (EPIC) and feasibility bounds
$\mathcal{U}_i(\theta_i)$ without revealing $\theta_i$ or internal state. The
cryptographic layer thus secures regional inputs while enabling global
verification.

\subsection{Autonomous Distributed MPC Core}

The global state $x_t \in \mathbb{R}^n$ evolves under decentralized controls
$u_{i,t}$ and bounded astrophysical noise $w_t$:
\[
x_{t+1} = f(x_t, u_{1,t}, \dots, u_{N,t}, w_t), \quad \|w_t\| \le \epsilon_w.
\]
Each region $i$ solves a local receding-horizon MPC subproblem over horizon $H$:
\[
u_{i,t}^* = \arg\min_{u_i \in \mathcal{U}_i(\theta_i)} J_i(x_t, u_i),
\]
subject to local dynamics, sovereignty-preserving feasibility sets
$\mathcal{U}_i(\theta_i)$, and EPIC constraints. Strategic veto thresholds
derived from $\theta_i$ ensure that no region is forced into non-incentive-
compatible actions. The aggregate control law is
\[
u_t^* = \text{col}(u_{1,t}^*, \dots, u_{N,t}^*).
\]

\subsection{Global Harmonization and Actuator Deployment Layer}

Verified controls $u_t^*$ are mapped to physical actuators across multiple
infrastructural domains:
\begin{itemize}
    \item energy grids (load balancing, generation dispatch),
    \item food logistics (routing, storage, distribution),
    \item financial buffers (liquidity, stabilization mechanisms),
    \item information channels (signal dissemination, narrative harmonization).
\end{itemize}
Actuator feasibility sets enforce:
\[
u_{i,t} \in \mathcal{U}_i(\theta_i),
\]
with hard sovereignty caps. If a proposed intervention exceeds a region's
feasibility radius $\phi(\theta_i)$, a strategic veto is automatically
triggered, and the corresponding control component is clipped or rejected prior
to execution.

\subsection{Decentralized Satellite Mesh Broadcast Layer}

A distributed orbital mesh network implements verification, consensus, and epoch
synchronization. At each epoch $t$:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Regions broadcast commitments $C_{i,t}$ and proofs $\pi_{i,t}$.
    \item The satellite mesh executes a verification kernel:
    \[
    \text{VerifyZK}(\pi_{i,t}) = 1 \quad \Rightarrow \quad u_{i,t} \text{ accepted}.
    \]
    \item Once a consensus threshold $\kappa \ge \frac{2}{3}N$ valid proofs is
    reached, the mesh aggregates and signs the global control vector $u_t^*$.
    \item The updated global state $x_{t+1}$ and epoch clock are broadcast:
    \[
    t \rightarrow t+1.
    \]
\end{enumerate}
This broadcast layer closes the loop, feeding verified, entropy-synchronized
state data back into the MPC core for the next horizon.

\subsection{Integrated Closed-Loop Runtime}

Together, these layers form a continuous autonomous intelligence loop:
\[
\text{Entropy} \rightarrow \text{Cryptography} \rightarrow \text{MPC} \rightarrow
\text{Actuators} \rightarrow \text{Orbital Mesh} \rightarrow t+1,
\]
with global stability guaranteed by a distributed Lyapunov framework and
empirically validated via Monte Carlo simulations. The architecture is thus
both formally rigorous and operationally executable at planetary scale.